{"w":[{"kind":"entry","entry":{"id":"msg-f-mwk2y94f","parentId":null,"type":"message","message":{"role":"user","timestamp":1794882925743,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are the executor of task #1, \"Seed task\". This is a session of its own: you have no memory of the conversation the task came from, and everything you need is here.\n\n## The task\n\nA task for the seed.\n\nIt came from the conversation \"Seed talk\" (id 1f63c758-79dd-4786-8066-c56ba83f7d8b); your result is posted there.\n\n## Where you work\n\nYou work in the project's directory, /tmp/eta-seed-home/seed-project, itself: your changes are made in place.\n\n## Reporting\n\n- comment_task posts a progress note or a question on the task.\n- When the work is done, or you cannot go on without the user, call finish_task with a summary: what you did, the result, and what the user should check. It moves the task to review and posts the summary in the conversation. A run that stops without calling it is reminded once, then fails.\n- The user may comment on the task while you work; their comments reach you as messages, and a comment left once this run has ended wakes another one, in this session. Other agents the user mentions on the task answer in its thread; their answers reach you while you work.\n- Merging (opening a pull request) is decided after review: do not merge into the main branch unless the task says to.\n- get_task shows the whole task with its timeline."}]},"seq":1,"timestamp":1794882925743}},{"kind":"value","op":"set","namespace":"eta.session.tip","key":"","value":"msg-f-mwk2y94f"}],"t":1794882925746}
